{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 28 October 2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 27 October 2025 and numbered HD/BG/08/PD01, HD/BG/08/PD02, HD/BG/08/PD 03, HD/BG/08/PD 03, HD/BG/08/PD 04, HD/BG/08/PD 05, Site Location Plan was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990. \r\nThe proposal, as submitted, cannot be considered permitted development under Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B and C of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), because the Local Planning Authority is not satisfied that the development would be lawful by virtue of Article 3(5). Article 3(5) requires the existing use of the dwelling to be lawful; however the dwelling has been unlawfully converted to a C4 House in Multiple Occupation. As a result, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the proposal complies with the requirements of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B and C. Accordingly, the development does not benefit from permitted development rights.\r\n"
  ],
